## Conventions

- **Never edit `docs/journal.md` by hand or from within a PR branch.** It's appended by `.github/workflows/claude.yml` *after* your PR merges, via `.github/scripts/journal-entry.sh`. Editing it in your branch means every open PR touches the same file and goes conflicting the moment any other PR merges.
- Follow NetBox plugin conventions (see https://docs.netbox.dev/en/stable/plugins/development/): subclass `netbox.plugins.PluginConfig`, not a plain Django `AppConfig`; use NetBox's base model/view/filterset classes where a NetBox equivalent exists.
- Verify NetBox APIs against the installed package rather than assuming them — the workflow's setup step installs a real NetBox into the runner specifically so imports and base classes can be checked locally instead of guessed, e.g.:

  ```
  python -c "import netbox.plugins as p; print(dir(p))"
  ```
- Model changes ship with their migration (`python manage.py makemigrations {{PYTHON_PACKAGE}}`), committed alongside the model change.
- Keep commit and PR scope to the files named in the issue or in the repo map above.
- {{ADDITIONAL_CONVENTIONS}}

## Definition of done

- The issue's acceptance criteria are met.
- Tests pass: `python manage.py test {{PYTHON_PACKAGE}}` (run from the NetBox install directory, plugin installed via `pip install -e .`).
- Lint is clean: `ruff check {{PYTHON_PACKAGE}}/` and `ruff format --check {{PYTHON_PACKAGE}}/`.
- Any shell script added is `bash -n`-clean and executable (`chmod +x`).
- Any JSON added is valid (`jq . <file>` succeeds).
- PR description explains what you implemented, what you verified, and anything you could not verify unattended.
